{
 "_doc": "The Maple Terraces (zen), generated by a script from the concept docs/concepts/zen-garden.webp. Phases: base fBm -> noise -> raise -> flatten (file order) -> paths -> carve/bowl -> water -> seams/border. The hill rises toward the north-west (a raise centred off the NW corner) and is cut into concentric terrace rings (ring_<height>, 3 m steps; the walled ones are steep, 4 m falloff). The main garden (31 m) is a built-up platform at x 194-296, z 925-1035, entered from the south up two stair flights (st_landing, st_garden) through the torii; the pagoda terrace is 6 m above it behind the temple (st_pagoda), a narrower terrace (e1) steps down on its east side, and the koi pond is two overlapping pools. Stair ramps are 0.5 m flatten strips under the zen_temple_steps props.",
